WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Press two fingertips to your
wrist, on the thumb side.

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.370
You feel a pulse.

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.710
Each pulse is a pressure wave.

4
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.840
Every time the ventricles contract, they
force a surge of blood into the arteries.

5
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.130
Yet in the capillaries beside your cells,

6
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.860
the surges are gone.

7
00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.530
Blood creeps past,
hundreds of times slower.

8
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.180
So how does a surging pump give
a steady trickle past every cell?

9
00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.190
In this mission, you'll compare the
walls of five kinds of blood vessel,

10
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.810
layer by layer.

11
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.290
Then you'll track blood pressure all
the way from the aorta to the veins.

12
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.220
Your mission: explain how blood leaving
the heart in surges trickles steadily

13
00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.480
past your cells.
